<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Entitlements for the Electron build signed with a real Apple Developer
    ID, the only shape Apple will notarize. The hardened runtime is on, and
    it denies everything not listed here.

    audio-input
        The microphone. The runtime process (resources/backend) opens the
        input device, not Electron, so the key has to be on the nested
        binary as well as the app; electron-builder signs nested code with
        the "inherit" file, which carries the same keys (see
        entitlements.mac.inherit.plist).

    allow-jit, allow-unsigned-executable-memory
        V8, in the main process and in the renderer and GPU helpers.
        Without them Electron aborts at launch under the hardened runtime.

    Deliberately absent: disable-library-validation. With a Developer ID
    every nested library carries the bundle's Team ID, so validation passes
    unaided and the key would turn off a real protection for nothing. The
    self-signed local build needs it and takes it from
    entitlements.mac.local.plist, the same split the Qt build makes with
    scripts/entitlements.plist and scripts/entitlements-local.plist.
    tests/test_desktop_packaging.py holds the difference.

    Accessibility and Microphone permissions are TCC grants the user makes;
    no entry here grants or bypasses either.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
